Third-party reference emulators
==============================

These files retain their upstream terms; the project's MIT and
CERN-OHL-W-2.0 grants do not relicense them.

superzazu_z80.{c,h}: MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Nicolas Allemand.
chips_z80.h: zlib, Copyright (c) 2021 Andre Weissflog.
suzukiplan_z80.hpp: MIT, Copyright (c) 2019 Yoji Suzuki.
redcode_z80/Z80.{c,h}: LGPL-3.0-or-later, Copyright (C) 1999-2026
    Manuel Sainz de Baranda y Goñi.
redcode_z80/Zeta/: LGPL v3 as stated in individual file headers;
    preserve all per-file authors and grants.
perfectz80/netlist_sim.c: MIT, Copyright (c) 2010,2014 Michael Steil,
    Brian Silverman, Barry Silverman.
Other perfectz80 files, particularly the generated netlist: retain
    upstream terms; exact licensing needs verification. Do not infer
    that the simulator's MIT notice licenses the entire directory.

See ../../THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for upstream links, the full inventory,
and provenance questions. Applicable license texts and copied notices
are in ../../LICENSES/ and ../../LICENSES/third-party/.

Preserve the license and copyright notices embedded in each source file.
